ream.remote.md:13:## 1. Invariant, impossibilities, non-goals\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:60:## 2. The design: mirror and reflection\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:91:### 2.1 Wire shapes\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:95:the transport-owned namespace rule of `dao.stream.md` (Envelopes).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:169:  Granularity). For a named request it carries the name, and an identity\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:177:### 2.2 The remote descriptor\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:188:contract's Envelopes section requires of descriptors for one logical stream\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:194:### 2.3 The mirror step\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:243:### 2.4 The reflection\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:352:### 2.5 Loss and resend\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:354:The reflection reads no clock. A link's `:dao.stream.remote/resend-after k`\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:368:## 3. Channels\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:375:### 3.1 WebSocket\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:407:### 3.2 UDP\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:423:  whole encoded datagram, fragment envelope included: at most 1200 bytes,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:428:  :dao.stream.udp/bytes b}`, where `n` is the carried message's own request\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:434:  composition data, `:dao.stream.udp/max-message-bytes` (default 64 KiB)\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:436:  message; no clock. Neither the mirror step nor the link sees a fragment.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:448:### 3.3 Pair\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:476:## 4. Reachability and NAT\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:530:## 5. Conventions that are not protocol\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:576:## 6. Lease integration\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:639:## 7. Middleware and the ShiBi seam\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md:667:## 8. Unification and contract boundary\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:1:# DaoStream Design\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:7:## Purpose\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:69:## Invariants\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:96:## Result Convention\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:134:## The IO Model\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:174:### Why this model and not the other two\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:190:### What it costs\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:200:### The readiness extension\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:216:## Creation and Attachment\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:259:### Envelopes\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:369:### Host Dispatch\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:405:## Surfaces\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:479:### Where the asynchrony goes\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:497:## Cursors\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:507:  transport-owned anchors (a byte offset, a timestamp). An anchor that is\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:565:## Reading\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:588:## Writing\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:623:## Close\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:673:## Concurrency\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:696:## Retention and Gaps\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:725:### Complete history\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:785:## Composition\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:805:## Explicitly Absent\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:836:## Open Decisions\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:848:*Result Convention*, *Writing*, *Envelopes* and *Cursors*; the numbers are\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:849:not reused. OD-4 is a paragraph today, while three transports and a handful\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:854:### OD-4. A logical stream can close but cannot end\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:894:### OD-5. \"No operation waits\" binds the seven operations and nothing above them\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:986:### Recorded, not proposed\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.md:1007:- **Granularity.** An element is a whole value; there is no byte offset within\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1:## §7. The Universal Continuation Format (Proposed)\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:25:# Universal Continuation Format — protocol draft\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:70:## §7.1 Stance: a continuation is a value, not a session\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:109:## §7.2 Vocabulary and envelope\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/d