ign/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1933:### 7.7.7 Restart\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1970:### 7.7.8 Fenced custody, version 1: sequence, envelope, epoch binding\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2010:   the same bytes, so from the same counter and the same carried\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2105:equal when their canonical bytes are equal. FFI and link correlation\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2212:  for the occurrence. Carrier bytes may remain as history, but a\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2262:   repaired. Any offered variant whose bytes verify to the recorded\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2295:offer in this order: inspect the bytes; under the authority lock,\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2350:## §7.8 Lifecycle: lift on park, lower on resume\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2412:## §7.9 Outcome algebra\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2449:  every other check but the bytes and the tag (7.2.1).\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2501:  BLAKE3 of the canonical bytes of `[:yin.k/append target value]`\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2504:  canonical-byte equality; the conflict decision is unchanged.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2542:## §7.10 Invariant compliance\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2562:## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase\n/Users/sto/wo